the ending of moon knight does some  heavy lifting to wrap up the season's  story and then at the last minute it  seriously pulls the rug out from under  the viewer's feet warning spoilers for  moon night episode six ahead  mark specter  stephen and grant  whoever else might be in there  as arthur harrow notes in moon knight  the head of mark spector stephen grant  is more than a little crowded by the  time the finale episode is over this  umpteenth little tease about another  personality's existence comes into play  in a major way despite the warnings of  taw eric mark spector turns back to his  peaceful field of reads and chooses to  rescue stephen from duot he still finds  a form of peace though after finally  confessing that he needs steven to keep  together and even calling the cheerful  brit identity his only true superpower a  pretty heavy statement from a guy who  wields powers granted by a moon god  with that mark and steven become whole  return to their body and become moon  knight and mr knight again unfortunately  even their combined forces aren't quite  enough to defeat hero who comes within  inches of killing mark however after  mark experiences another unexplained  mid-fight blackout it's hero who lies  helpless on the ground  at this point even the most casual  viewer probably suspects that a third  unseen identity is responsible for  knocking harrow's glass-filled shoes off  his feet after all the show has teased  this dangerous persona's existence since  episode three  stephen what did you do i swear it  wasn't me then who was it  by the time the post-credits scene comes  along the jake lockley identity indeed  makes his presence known wearing his  signature flat cap the violent jake  hijacks hero from the hospital and  shoots him while konshu looks on in this  short scene this new persona establishes  himself as a ruthless and capable  operator what's worse he's still  willingly working with konshu and since  he occupies the same body as stephen and  mark it appears that none of them are as  free from the lunar god's servitude as  they think moon knight has been teasing  the possibility that leila el puli might  become the new avatar of konchu for a  while and while she does gain  avatar-based superpowers in episode 6  this happens in a very different way  than you might think sure the show  teases a leila as moon knight moment  when she releases kanchu from his mini  statue prison and the moon god offers to  make her his new avatar leila promptly  refuses and even attempts to browbeat  konchu into partnership instead of a  servitude deal this doesn't go  particularly well but as it turns out  this isn't the first time layla cold  shoulders and egyptian gods avatar  offered that day  only an avatar can do it  i said  no  earlier in the episode tara delivers  mark's message to layla and throws in a  far less ominous avatar deal in the  process wary of mark's negative  experiences layla initially turns  tarrara down but reconsiders upon  learning that team egyptian pantheon  needs more avatars to successfully trap  amit as such she accepts the hippo  goddess's offer this proves to be a good  call because the delighted to eric  provides layla with some welcome  information about her father's afterlife  situation and grants her a cool winged  costume  wow you look amazing what are you  wearing  layla appears to highly enjoy her new  avatar powers what's more the show  pretty much states that she's not going  anywhere anytime soon when a young girl  asks whether she's an egyptian superhero  and layla immediately confirms that she  is just like that moon knight has  delivered the origin story of a  character who's been confirmed to be the  scarlet scarab making her debut in the  mcu  harrow continues his penance-filled path  in this episode of moon knight and his  mission to let amit clean the world  keeps adding to the show's body count  after pulling assorted don't resist and  you don't get hurt stunts including one  on the egyptian gods avatars he finally  releases the crocodile-headed judgment  deity who probably makes hero her  official avatar from this point on  things play out very much like harold  promised in episode 1. emmett's  followers start cleansing the world and  the goddess feasts on the souls of  scales deem unworthy unfortunately for  the villains the plan is rudely  interrupted by the freshly resurrected  moon knight and the taoiret powered  layla who managed to defeat hero and  trap amit in his body the shock is  enough to hospitalize hero but even then  he finds no peace despite amit's  promises instead jake lockley  unceremoniously abducts and shoots him  destroying amits in the process  it's not exactly a surprise that the  villain loses in the end but the way  episode vi presents harrow as a  vulnerable hurt and deeply regretful man  who's simply going through his twisted  perception of doing the right thing is a  pretty nice take for an mcu antagonist  by the time he's forced to act as amit's  living broken vessel hero has clearly  endured so much pain that even the  hitherto implacable dr harrell construct  in mark's mind is hurt and terrified  few mcu properties can escape the big  cgi ending battle so by the time harrow  stands on the pyramid and moon knight is  flying around it's clear that moon  knight is about to deliver on this front  instead of the harrow moon knight  showdown that you might have been  expecting though the show turns his  ultimate battle into a full-on super  team fight moon knight keeps alternating  between his main costume and steven's mr  knight persona the freshly advertised  leila soon turns up to help and harold's  cultist keeps stirring the pot in the  background ammit and konchu keep  themselves busy with a kaiju sized  grudge match this goes pretty much as  you'd expect after almost getting  defeated the good guys ultimately win  the night and even steven gets to  demonstrate some sweet moves however  this being moon night the real battle is  just beginning and ultimately inside  mark's head as the post-credits scene  reveals kanju is taken to deploying  mark's third personality jake as his  secret avatar which effectively renders  his release of mark and steven  completely moot as they share the same  body  and so like cycles of the moon the  protagonist ends where he began in  steven's messy london apartment when the  confused main character's leg chained to  his bed and a futile attempt to stop  blackout walking and the same song  playing in the background meanwhile a  mysterious violent personality is making  moves out in the world  moon knight doesn't shy away from the  fact that konchu isn't the nicest or  most effective deity around as everyone  from harrow to layla is quick to point  out he's an abusive and treacherous  entity at the best of times and kanchu  himself is quick to confirm all the  negative reviews with his condescending  attitude overly theatrical delivery and  rampant name calling it doesn't exactly  help the moon god's case that he manages  to get himself trapped in a statue  halfway through the show and starts  throwing shade at layla the second she  releases him the end of moon knight  episode 6 however features copious consu  action and makes it clear that the deity  is far more than a pompous poser not  only does he fearlessly engage the  dangerous ammet in combat on two  separate occasions but he also reveals  himself as a kind of ruthless trickster  that loki would be proud of his interest  in laila as a potential future avatar  was a faint all along and the moon god  has actually been working with mark's  jake lockley identity to ensure that he  stays in conscious service though kanchu  is technically fighting evil it  certainly seems that he's no angel  himself and may actually be outright  dangerous he's extremely dedicated to  keeping mark steven jake as his avatar  and his final scene in the episode hints  at this obsession is about to turn  hostile not only does he outright  declare that mark's troubles have only  just begun but his new sweet suit  resembles the outfit he wears in the  jeff lemire pen moon knight comics where  konchu is the villain  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the marvel cinematic universe are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]

